@startuml hovered-page-states
' The arbiter's record of the page host under the pointer (`hovered`), and
' what each transition does to the pages. Colours: blue = the pointer is over
' the chrome, purple = over a page.
skinparam defaultFontName "Noto Sans"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam state {
  BorderColor #52687A
  ArrowColor #52687A
  FontColor #182734
}
title Pointer hover across the chrome and its pages

state "Over the chrome" as OverChrome #DDEBF7
OverChrome : hovered = None
OverChrome : cursor: that of the chrome element under the pointer

state "Over page P" as OverPage #E4DFEC
OverPage : hovered = P's host
OverPage : cursor: that of P's element under the pointer
OverPage : <b>Without leaving P:</b>
OverPage : · the pointer moves in P, or P is laid out again
OverPage : (refresh_hover): P reports dirty, the cursor is recomputed
OverPage : · a new document replaces P (page_attached): it is seeded
OverPage : · the hover moves onto another page Q: clear P, seed Q

[*] --> OverChrome
OverChrome --> OverPage : the chrome's hover moves onto P's host\n(a pointer event, or a layout change:\ntab switch, sidebar toggle)\n<b>seed P</b>: set_hover_to(pointer in P's coordinates)
OverPage --> OverChrome : the chrome's hover leaves P's host\n<b>clear P</b>: clear_hover() ends :hover\nand forgets P's pointer position
OverPage --> OverChrome : P's host is removed (tab closed)\n<b>forget it</b>: view_removed (node ids are reused)

note right of OverPage
  Every sync ends the same way:
  cursor = window_cursor(get_cursor(), hidden_by_css),
  and the window is told only when it changed.
  Seeding and clearing change hover state only:
  no DOM event is dispatched, as with Blitz's refresh_hover.
end note
@enduml
